# Copy to .env (compose reads it automatically from this directory).
# Everything here is optional.

# -- Edge ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public hostname the Traefik router matches. It must be the same hostname the
# Cloudflare tunnel publishes (dashboard -> tunnel -> public hostnames), and it
# is also handed to DSH as `--trusted-host`, so the deployment declares the
# authority browsers actually use.
# DSH_PUBLIC_HOST=harness.itsrose.my.id

# -- In-container Basic Auth (optional, usually left empty) -----------------
# Access is meant to be gated by Cloudflare Access (Zero Trust) at the edge.
# Set BOTH only if you want a second gate that still works when the edge policy
# is absent, permissive, or being debugged. One without the other is treated as
# "no auth" by the upstream proxy. When both are empty, anyone who reaches the
# hostname drives an agent with a shell in ./workspace -- make sure the tunnel
# policy, not the obscurity of the hostname, is what stops them.
# DSH_PROXY_USER=
# DSH_PROXY_PASS=

# -- Optional overrides -----------------------------------------------------
# Pin a different published base image (default: devtools-min-0.2.2-rc.1).
# DSH_BASE_IMAGE=smanx/deepseek-harness:devtools-min-0.2.2-rc.1
# Tag of the image built from ./Dockerfile.
# DSH_IMAGE=dsh-harness:nonroot
# Force a permission mode instead of probing: read-only | workspace-write |
# danger-full-access. Leave empty to let the entrypoint detect a backend.
# DSH_PERMISSION_MODE=
# Seconds to wait for DSH before giving up (first boot downloads the profile).
# DSH_READY_TIMEOUT=600
# TZ=Asia/Jakarta
